From bbd1c96d5998a7db7d30ba985fbbc8cb59b79166 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shaun Adams <s.adams@f5.com>
Date: Fri, 12 Jun 2026 21:39:45 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 19/42] transports+configstore: POST
 /api/tenants/{tenant_id}/mcp/clients (admin create per-tenant MCP)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Completes the per-tenant inference plane: providers (patch 0016) +
VKs (patch 0017) + MCP (this patch) is the minimum set the user
needs to drive /v1/chat/completions and /v1/mcp/tool/execute on a
per-tenant basis.

configstore additions:
- ConfigStore.GetMCPConfigByTenant(ctx, tenantID) returns only MCP
  clients whose tenant_id matches. Empty tenantID normalizes to
  DefaultTenantID, matching the existing providers-by-tenant policy.
  Shared with GetMCPConfig via a private getMCPConfigInternal helper.
- ConfigStore.CreateMCPClientConfigForTenant(ctx, tenantID, config)
  pins tenantID on the new TableMCPClient row so it is only visible
  to GetMCPConfigByTenant(tenantID). Shared with CreateMCPClientConfig
  via createMCPClientConfigInternal. Uniqueness check is now
  (tenant_id, name) — two tenants can both register an MCP client
  called "tools".
- MockConfigStore updated.
- Tests covering: tenant_id write isolation, two tenants same MCP name
  via composite uniqueness.

Transport additions:
- handlers.TenantMCPHandler with POST /api/tenants/{tenant_id}/mcp/clients.
  Minimum-viable payload (id optional, name + connection_type required,
  optional connection_string), mints a UUID if no id is supplied,
  calls CreateMCPClientConfigForTenant, evicts the per-tenant runtime.
  Tests covering: happy path, explicit id pass-through, missing-name,
  missing-connection-type, missing-tenant-ctx, nil-store rejection.
- Wires into server.go alongside the other tenant-scoped handlers.
- The per-tenant Bifrost runtime loader in buildInferenceRouter now
  also loads MCPConfig via GetMCPConfigByTenant so a fresh Acquire
  picks up the tenant's MCP clients without a process restart.

Layer 1 integration test extended to provision an MCP client per
tenant with the same name "tools" but distinct connection strings,
then assert GetMCPConfigByTenant returns the right one for each tenant
(would catch any cross-tenant leakage at the storage layer).

Out of scope: GET / PUT / DELETE on /api/tenants/{tid}/mcp/clients,
OAuth flow + admin-login + tool-discovery shape from the legacy
/api/mcp/client endpoint, allowed-extra-headers, tool pricing. Those
follow once Phase 4's AuthzPlugin resolves a real tenant-admin caller.

Ref: https://jira.f5net.com/browse/XC-25496
